# TestOval - a hand-written track, with banked corners and two jumps.
#
#   python3 tools/trackc.py compile Tracks/TestOval.trk
#   ./stuntcarracer --track Tracks/TestOval.bin
#
# CORNERS
# -------
# There are two curve pieces of each hand.  "right" is 8 segments with a
# steering amount of 0x3e; "right9" is 9 segments at 0x32.  Both turn 45
# degrees, so right9 takes the same corner over a longer arc - a wider radius.
# None of the eight stock tracks turns a plain 90 degree corner with anything
# but a right9/left9 pair; "right"/"left" only ever appear coming out of a
# diagonal run.  Use right9 for corners.
#
# BANKING
# -------
# A bank is the two rails at different heights, so you make one by giving them
# different profiles.  Stock tracks bank symmetrically - the left rail up by
# the same amount the right comes down - so the middle of the road stays where
# it was and only the cross-slope changes.  "3/4" raises the left rail 512 and
# drops the right 512 (a 1024 bank); "4/3" takes it out again.  A flat "0"
# holds each rail where it is, so the corner itself can just be "right9 0"
# and it keeps the bank built on the piece before.
#
# These are right-hand corners, so the LEFT rail is the outside - that is the
# one that goes up.  For a left-hand corner you would bank "4/3" then "3/4".
#
# Every bank has to be undone before the lap ends, or the track will not close
# in height.

track   TestOval
start   3          # a flat piece - piece 0 is the ramp off the last corner
boost   34 47
origin  2,2 +Z
# The lap starts on the piece coming OUT of the last corner, so it starts
# already banked: left rail 512 up, right rail 512 down.
height  1792 768

# Brake the opponent into the two jumps.
speed   2  0x58 runup
speed   18 0x58 runup

# ---- north straight: level out, jump, then bank into the corner ----
# This first piece takes the bank off the LAST corner - the lap wraps.
straight    4/3
straight    0
straight    0
straight    0
straight    0
straight    3/4
# ---- banked corner (the flat 0s hold the bank) ----
right9      0
right9      0            light
# ---- east straight ----
straight    4/3
straight    0
straight    0
straight    0
straight    0
straight    3/4
# ---- banked corner ----
right9      0
right9      0            light
# ---- south straight, with the second jump ----
straight    4/3
straight    0
straight    0
straight    0
straight    0
straight    3/4
# ---- banked corner ----
right9      0
right9      0            light
# ---- west straight ----
straight    4/3
straight    0
straight    0
straight    0
straight    0
straight    3/4
# ---- banked corner ----
right9      0
right9      0            light
